      "math_academy_id": "q-71858",
      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "Given the hyperboloid of one sheet $\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(z-3)^{2}}{9}=1$, find its $y$-intercepts.",
      "worked_solution": "To find the $y$-intercepts, we plug $x=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(0-2)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(0-3)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ 1+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}-1 & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =4 \\\\ y-2 & =\\pm \\sqrt{4} \\\\ y & =2\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $y=0$ and $y=4.$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $y$-axis are $(0,0,0)$ and $(0,4,0).$",
